description:
FILED BY worker-0520a42e FROM task-33ceae56edc348e9864bc592430fa1d0 (SPIDR child 3, the Gate 2 browser proof) at step 1, 2026-09-06. Global rail 20 (spun-out rows) and global rail 4 clause 1 (a pure package is not finished until one real consumer edge exists).

THE GAP, MEASURED AT HEAD eb13d2f6 ON moe/work-2026-09-04. Epic rail 1 says a command kind is a FOUR-ROW job: shared contract + digest mirrors; the refusal vocabulary; DAEMON WIRING AND OPERATOR FENCE; then the behaviour. The Gate 2 band shipped rows 1, 2, the FENCE HALF of row 3, and row 4's runner package - but nothing ever wired the runner into the daemon. The release band has its equivalent row explicitly (task-54b74b80 "release.decide is wired in the daemon registry"); Gate 2 has none. This row is that missing third row.

FOUR INDEPENDENT MEASUREMENTS, each reproducible:

(1) THE REGISTRY ENTRY IS AN UNCONDITIONAL FAIL-CLOSED STUB. apps/daemon/src/daemon-command-registry.ts:430-439. Its own comment says so: "The second throw is the FAIL-CLOSED stub the runner replaces."
      if (preview) {
        const decoded = decodePreviewDecidePayload(envelope.payload);
        if (!decoded.ok) {
          throw new DomainRefusal(decoded.code, decoded.layer, "preview.decide payload refused");
        }
        const stub = previewRefusal("PREVIEW_GOAL_NOT_LANDED");
        throw new DomainRefusal(stub.code, stub.layer, "preview runner is not landed");
      }
EVERY well-formed preview.decide - APPROVE or REJECT - throws PREVIEW_GOAL_NOT_LANDED @ GOAL_AUTHORITY. No decision is ever committed and none can be read back from /activity/read.

(2) THE RUNNER PACKAGE HAS ZERO CONSUMERS. `git grep -n "preview/preview-" -- '*.ts' '*.tsx' '*.js' ':!*/dist/*' ':!apps/daemon/src/preview/*'` returns exactly FOUR hits, all importing ONLY ./preview/preview-contracts.js (the vocabulary): daemon-command-families.ts:21, daemon-command-payload-keys.ts:34, daemon-command-registry.ts:28, daemon-command-vocabulary.ts:26. `git grep -n "createPreviewRunner|createPreviewSupervisor|previewReceiptId"` outside apps/daemon/src/preview/ returns ZERO. preview-runner, preview-supervisor, preview-ledger, preview-capture, preview-process, preview-receipt-contracts, preview-goal-landing and preview-command-resolution are unreachable from the live daemon.

(3) NOTHING CAN START A PREVIEW. preview.decide is the ONLY preview command kind on the roster (packages/contracts/src/runtime/runtime-vocabulary.ts:104). `git grep -n "preview\.start"` over apps/ and packages/ returns ZERO. `runPreview` therefore has no trigger: no command, no goal-lifecycle hook, no HTTP route. No receipt is ever written to a live store, so `moe-preview-receipt/1` (preview-receipt-contracts.ts:47) exists only inside its own package's tests.

(4) preview.decide IS NOT ON THE AFFORDANCE OFFER SURFACE. `git grep -in "preview" -- 'apps/daemon/src/http/affordance-*.ts'` excluding tests returns ZERO. The browser is never offered the decision, so no Needs-you card can render even if a receipt existed. (The affordance-planning-offers.test.ts:456 hit is HUMAN_ONLY_STEPS membership - the fence - not an offer.)

WHAT THIS ROW MUST DELIVER, at minimum, for the Gate 2 proof row to be reachable:
(a) Replace the registry stub with a real edge that calls into the landed runner/ledger, so APPROVE commits a durable decision and REJECT records its findings. Keep every refusal minted through `previewRefusal` so code and layer cannot disagree (preview-contracts.ts derives layer from PREVIEW_CODE_LAYERS).
(b) A way to START a preview for a landed goal, whose completion writes a receipt via `recordPreviewReceipt`. Whether that is a new operator kind, a goal-lifecycle hook or a dispatcher step is this row's design call - but epic rail 1 and 2 bind: a NEW runtime command kind means the shared contract, ALL FOUR GENERATED_CONTRACT_DIGEST mirrors, the regenerated client, and `pnpm --filter @moe/control-room test`.
(c) OFFER preview.decide on the affordance surface for a goal whose receipt is STARTED, targeted at that goal, so the browser can see it. It is already human-only (HUMAN_ONLY_STEPS, agent-spawn-contract.ts:229) and MCP-excluded, so the fence needs no change - only the offer.
(d) Wire `createPreviewSupervisor().close()` into daemon shutdown: task-f5a74c23's handoff names that as "the daemon-shutdown seam a composition row should call", and it is the arm that row was permitted to leave uncovered.

DO NOT re-implement the runner. It is landed, tested (7 files / 93 tests under src/preview, exit 0) and correct; commit 6de79b6cb074d4a02f89b862727eb0f9c789153b. This row is a COMPOSITION row: it adds the edges, not the behaviour.

CONTENTION WARNING (epic rail 3): daemon-command-registry.ts, daemon-command-families.ts and daemon-command-vocabulary.ts are the shared rosters every concurrent kind-publishing row on this epic touches (task-a2409cba, task-c422b106, task-166d375f). Never freeze a roster COUNT literal - run the leg and take the PRINTED expected-vs-received as authoritative.
